  "negative_evidence": [
    "Initial 14-case baseline: 13 assertion failures and one pass. Final 16-case baseline: 15 assertion failures and one pass; no test errors, skips or cancellations.",
    "Session-body error normalization already passed; no new defect is claimed in that path.",
    "Application callback exceptions retain their identity; they are outside the transport diagnostic normalization boundary.",
    "Checkpoints do not preempt synchronous work or terminate arbitrary sources that ignore abort; five-second test watchdogs are not deployment deadlines.",
    "Two EAGAIN host spawn failures while reading policy recovered on retry; earlier read-only FETCH_HEAD prevents claiming a refreshed main.",
    "Initial endpoint trust, lexical-number forms and producer whole-event size reconciliation remain open. Remote deletion remains best effort."
  ],
  "security_review": "Fixed transport errors contain no original rejection value or cause. Native caller cancellation at headers/body and before POST is exercised. Same-chunk cancellation stops before the next parsed event. Existing renderer identity, validated-handle binding and independent DELETE controls pass. No authority, identity storage, dependencies or server changes.",
